Android changes to virglrenderer 1.3.0 for the Andronix app (standalone mode).
Adapted from Termux's virglrenderer-android recipe (MIT, like virglrenderer):
- meson.build: Android has EGL without GBM; no memfd_create/timespec_get
  detection (bionic has them only from API 30/29; we build for API 26);
  clang's GNU-extension warnings off.
- detect_os.h: an NDK build, not AOSP (Mesa's Android paths need
  log/log.h and cutils).
- vrend_winsys.c: EGL on the default display (pbuffer + GLES) on Android.
- vrend_winsys_egl.c: on Android, GLES needs neither EGL_KHR_create_context
  nor EGL_KHR_surfaceless_context; without the latter (EGL 1.4 drivers, the
  emulator), contexts are made current on a 1x1 pbuffer; the config says
  ES3 (vrend's contexts are GLES 3.x; EGL_BAD_MATCH otherwise).
- vrend_renderer.c: no dual-source blending on Android (draws wrong on
  Adreno: virglrenderer issue 223).
- vtest_server.c: on Android, try the renderer once in a forked child
  before listening, and exit if the phone's EGL/GLES can't run it (the app
  then starts the desktop in software, not black).
- vrend_renderer.c, fast readback (on by default; VTEST_FAST_READBACK=0
  turns it off): every X11 window's frame is a B8G8R8[AX]8 readback, which
  on GLES went through a fresh full-frame malloc, a CPU swizzle and a second
  copy. It now reads straight into the guest's memory: BGRA where
  GL_EXT_read_format_bgra exists, else RGBA swizzled in place; a flipped one
  copies once from a kept buffer. A GL error on the first fast readback
  turns it off for good and the frame is read the old way. Device Farm
  (gpu3 scenes, 800x600): glmark2 +15% to +26% on Pixel 4a, Pixel 8, A15,
  S24 Ultra; GPU now ahead of software on all four.
- andronix_present.c (new), vrend_renderer.c, src/meson.build: zero-copy
  present. When the app passes VTEST_PRESENT_SOCKET and
  VTEST_PRESENT_SIZE_FILE (one "W H" line per window size it can show: the
  full screen, and windows of a unique size that nothing covers), a
  display-target readback of one of those sizes is a GPU blit into one of
  three AHardwareBuffers the app shows at the window's place, with a native
  fence where the driver has one (else glFinish); no readback, no Xvfb copy,
  no upload. A size the app stops listing (a menu opened over the window)
  goes back to the readback within 100 ms. The app replaces the list file
  atomically (temporary file, then rename), so the server always reads a
  whole list. Any failure
  drops back to the readback; three failed connections in a row and that
  client stays on the readback. Device Farm (full screen, glmark2 gpu3
  scenes): +16% Pixel 4a, +47% Pixel 8, +19% A15, +38% S24 Ultra over the
  fast readback. Protocol at the top of the file.
- vtest_shm.c: memfd_create, else ASharedMemory_create (apps targeting
  Android 10+ may not open /dev/ashmem).

